# Keep working-tree bytes identical on every platform. The index stores LF;
# with core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites everything to CRLF, so
# recorded SHA-256 values only matched when they had been taken on that same
# kind of checkout. Docker/ECS builds are Linux and expect LF as well.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A few recorded artifacts were hashed from CRLF working copies (the earlier
# Windows checkout, later bind-mounted into Linux containers). Their recorded
# hashes are evidence and must not be rewritten, so pin those exact files to
# CRLF on every platform. All other hashed fixtures and evidence (for example
# tests/fixtures/motis-v2.11.2/real-plan-depart-at.json) are LF.
poc/corpora/places-venues.json text eol=crlf
poc/corpora/places.json text eol=crlf
poc/routing/config.yml text eol=crlf
